@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Lost & Found — Mahidol University
+
+Static pages hosted on GitHub Pages, backed by a Google Apps Script web app and Google Sheets.
+
+## Data flow
+
+The Thai and English forms submit to Apps Script, which saves new records in `LF_New`, uploads images to Drive and calls existing LINE/email notification code. Legacy Google Form records remain in `Form Responses`. Gallery, admin list, Dashboard and PDF export read the combined `getAllData` response.
+
+## October 2026 fixes
+
+- Shared `assets/lf-data.js` parses UTC/offset ISO timestamps as instants and historical unzoned strings as Bangkok time. Calendar filters, report grouping and visible dates use `Asia/Bangkok`.
+- All six consuming pages load the shared script. Form date/time defaults follow Bangkok, including before 07:00.
+- Concurrent reads in one page share one request; failed, invalid and timed-out responses surface an error while existing records remain visible. Gallery background refresh preserves its existing content.
+- Gallery labels the timestamp as the submission time. The incident date/time remains a separate field in the Sheet.
+- No raw report or contact data is persisted to browser storage by the shared data module.
+
+Run regression checks with Node.js 22 or later:
+
+```text
+node tests/data.test.cjs
+```
+
+Repeat under `Asia/Bangkok`, `UTC`, and `America/Los_Angeles` using the `TZ` environment variable. Optional `LF_API_FIXTURE` points to a private local `getAllData` response; never commit that fixture.
+
+## Apps Script cache proposal — separate deployment
+
+`apps-script/get-all-data-cache.gs` is a replacement for the existing `getAllData` function, with internal helpers. It has not been installed in the live Apps Script project by this frontend change. Remove the existing function before inserting the replacement; do not add a duplicate function definition.
+
+It caches compressed JSON in ASCII chunks smaller than the Apps Script per-entry limit. Cache entries are scoped to a 30-second time bucket; missing chunks or service errors fall back to the Sheet. Manual refresh sends `force=1` to bypass the cache. This is not pagination and does not reduce response payload size. Benchmark after deploying and check the deployed source against current project code before creating a new version.
+
+## Priority follow-up work
+
+1. Replace browser-side shared-password checks with server-side authentication and authorization. Existing mutation actions must validate the authenticated user. Do not place new secrets in this public repository.
+2. Split public item data from staff contact/details endpoints. The current public API sends names, phone numbers and internal fields.
+3. Escape untrusted fields before inserting HTML; render user text with `textContent` and validate image URLs.
+4. Use one reporting dataset for old and new forms. Generate the previous month's final report on the first day of the next month; prevent duplicate report/notification delivery.
+5. Confirm successful persistence before showing form success. Add idempotency keys, a server-generated case ID, input validation and upload limits.
+6. Protect append-and-follow-up row updates against concurrent submissions using a lock or stable-ID row lookup.
+7. Queue LINE/email delivery, record attempts/results, and retry independently of the form response. Existing best-effort code still runs synchronously.
+8. Add server-side filters/pagination and a summary endpoint; consider a database only when measured load and workflow justify migration.
+
+Current account trigger review found legacy handlers assigned to spreadsheet-open events. Review with their owners before removal. No notification test was sent during the audit.
